  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the most critical uncertainty is establishing a performance baseline against which all other design choices can be evaluated. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest, most interpretable configuration: a single modality, a single profile (no aggregation needed), and PCA—a standard, well-understood linear encoder. This experiment will (1) reveal the baseline accuracy/F1 achievable from RNA data alone with a straightforward pipeline, (2) serve as a reference floor so that subsequent experiments can quantify the incremental contribution of each design axis (image modality, learned encoders, multiprofile aggregation, fusion strategy), and (3) confirm that the pipeline runs correctly before investing budget in more complex configurations. Under a limited budget, anchoring the search with the cleanest possible baseline is the highest-information-value first step, as it reduces uncertainty about the entire design space simultaneously."
}

